1
00:01:43,110 --> 00:01:48,009
[When I Meet The Moon]

2
00:01:48,070 --> 00:01:51,200
[Episode 3]

3
00:01:52,370 --> 00:01:53,999
Has the passphrase been changed?

4
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,089
I'll call Xia.

5
00:01:55,090 --> 00:01:56,090
Try again.

6
00:01:58,070 --> 00:01:59,070
Come on.

7
00:02:01,370 --> 00:02:02,570
Puppy, open the door.

8
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:03,840
Louder.

9
00:02:08,430 --> 00:02:09,430
Puppy...

10
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:37,840
W-Why are you here?

11
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:40,470
Shouldn't I be here?

12
00:02:44,650 --> 00:02:45,210
Uncle,

13
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:46,630
has the lock been fixed?

14
00:02:47,870 --> 00:02:48,870
Yeah.

15
00:02:50,770 --> 00:02:51,999
-Little Kid? -Old Auntie?

16
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
-Why are you here? -Why are you here?

17
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:57,570
Tangy, you're here.

18
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:00,800
What's wrong?

19
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:01,870
What happened?

20
00:03:02,010 --> 00:03:03,810
-Something's wrong. -Nothing.

21
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:05,389
You know each other?

22
00:03:05,390 --> 00:03:06,390
-No. -Yes.

23
00:03:09,130 --> 00:03:10,590
You guys are quite in sync.

24
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:12,100
Tangy, don't mind him.

25
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:13,900
My brother is just like this.

26
00:03:14,970 --> 00:03:16,579
It's a small world.

27
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:19,280
I won't stoop to a little kid's level.

28
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:22,369
I won't stoop to

29
00:03:22,370 --> 00:03:23,679
an old auntie's level either.

30
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:24,680
You...

31
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:26,869
Alright, whether you
know each other or not,

32
00:03:26,870 --> 00:03:28,470
let me make an introduction.

33
00:03:28,710 --> 00:03:29,180
Hello,

34
00:03:29,181 --> 00:03:30,240
I'm Xia Congsheng.

35
00:03:30,470 --> 00:03:31,529
You must be Yun Li.

36
00:03:31,530 --> 00:03:33,260
I often hear Tangy mention you.

37
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:35,130
Hello.

38
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:36,680
This is my brother, Fu Zhengchu.

39
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:39,400
We met at the airport, remember?

40
00:03:40,590 --> 00:03:41,970
Sorry about last time.

41
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:43,578
I misunderstood you.

42
00:03:43,579 --> 00:03:44,370
It's fine.

43
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:46,060
You two know each other too?

44
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:47,090
Well...

45
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:48,529
The guy playing cool just now

46
00:03:48,530 --> 00:03:49,840
is my uncle, Fu Shize.

47
00:03:49,870 --> 00:03:50,870
Fu Shize?

48
00:03:51,130 --> 00:03:52,130
Isn't he your...
Please,

49
00:03:52,430 --> 00:03:53,630
d-don't say any more.

50
00:03:57,660 --> 00:04:00,320
You look like you're the same age.

51
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:02,630
How could he be your uncle?

52
00:04:02,870 --> 00:04:04,476
We're about the same age,
but my uncle's side

53
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:05,500
is senior to ours.

54
00:04:07,190 --> 00:04:07,970
Let's go inside.

55
00:04:07,971 --> 00:04:09,469
Don't just stand here chatting.

56
00:04:09,470 --> 00:04:10,470
Let's go in.

57
00:04:11,130 --> 00:04:12,130
Please come in.

58
00:04:12,470 --> 00:04:13,470
Let's go.

59
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:15,400
Don't follow me.

60
00:04:16,690 --> 00:04:17,690
How is it?
Not bad, right?

61
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:19,300
My little courtyard.

62
00:04:24,070 --> 00:04:24,870
Xia,

63
00:04:24,930 --> 00:04:26,240
what were you doing?

64
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:29,330
I was making crepe rolls,

65
00:04:29,430 --> 00:04:31,080
but they're too hard to make.

66
00:04:31,110 --> 00:04:33,489
I've been trying all morning
and haven't gotten anywhere.

67
00:04:33,490 --> 00:04:34,170
Our Lili

68
00:04:34,190 --> 00:04:35,620
is an expert in this.

69
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:37,100
Show her.

70
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:42,099
You overwhipped the egg whites.

71
00:04:42,100 --> 00:04:44,299
And if the crepe breaks like this,

72
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:46,269
the pan might be too hot,

73
00:04:46,270 --> 00:04:48,130
or the crepe has been overcooked.

74
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:49,180
Let me have a try.
Uncle,

75
00:04:50,070 --> 00:04:52,130
don't forget to fix the air purifier.

76
00:04:57,260 --> 00:04:58,370
L-Let me have a try.

77
00:04:58,560 --> 00:04:59,560
Okay.

78
00:05:53,330 --> 00:05:54,330
Lili,

79
00:05:54,630 --> 00:05:55,540
your crepe rolls

80
00:05:55,541 --> 00:05:57,070
look so beautiful!

81
00:05:58,570 --> 00:05:59,739
Our Lili is an expert

82
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:00,800
in this field.

83
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:02,100
Besides crepe rolls,

84
00:06:02,101 --> 00:06:04,190
she can make a lot of other desserts.

85
00:06:04,330 --> 00:06:05,330
Amazing.

86
00:06:05,630 --> 00:06:06,570
My job

87
00:06:06,571 --> 00:06:08,700
is to learn a little bit of everything.

88
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:11,310
It looks delicious!

89
00:06:15,570 --> 00:06:16,570
It's tasty!

90
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:18,480
It's really good.

91
00:06:18,481 --> 00:06:20,539
Better than the ones bought in stores.

92
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:21,540
Really?

93
00:06:23,770 --> 00:06:25,070
How did you two meet?

94
00:06:26,830 --> 00:06:27,800
When I went back to Nanwu,

95
00:06:27,801 --> 00:06:29,389
I bumped into Lili at the airport.

96
00:06:29,390 --> 00:06:30,370
I asked her to add me on WeChat,

97
00:06:30,371 --> 00:06:31,740
but she turned me down.

98
00:06:31,780 --> 00:06:33,600
I told her that EAW

99
00:06:33,630 --> 00:06:35,100
was run by Qingsong.

100
00:06:35,130 --> 00:06:36,590
But she didn't believe me.

101
00:06:37,070 --> 00:06:40,370
So Mr. Xu is really your brother?

102
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,430
We are sort of relatives.

103
00:06:42,570 --> 00:06:43,300
My great-aunt

104
00:06:43,301 --> 00:06:45,300
is Qingsong's adoptive godmother.

105
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:46,370
Uncle, it's delicious.

106
00:06:46,690 --> 00:06:47,690
Have a try.

107
00:06:58,600 --> 00:06:59,600
Is it good?

108
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:03,929
-I told you it's delicious. -Lili,

109
00:07:03,930 --> 00:07:05,129
come over often when you're free,

110
00:07:05,130 --> 00:07:07,060
so I can learn a few skills from you.

111
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:10,299
She's here to do a shop tour video.

112
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,700
How could she come often?

113
00:07:11,770 --> 00:07:12,430
Lili is going

114
00:07:12,431 --> 00:07:14,290
to study for her master's at NUST.

115
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:15,500
She's not going back.

116
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:16,740
Lili,

117
00:07:17,130 --> 00:07:18,180
we are alumni.

118
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:19,970
You should call her Senior.

119
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:21,239
That would sound too distant,

120
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:22,240
right, Lili?

121
00:07:24,570 --> 00:07:26,420
Have you found a place to live?

122
00:07:26,770 --> 00:07:27,630
Not yet.

123
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:28,919
Tangy and I are planning

124
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:30,329
to go house-hunting tomorrow.

125
00:07:30,330 --> 00:07:31,759
Why bother looking for a place?

126
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:32,899
I have so many rooms here.

127
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:34,590
Just pick one and move in.

128
00:07:35,740 --> 00:07:37,540
Xia, stop joking.

129
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:39,119
Lili is still a student

130
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,380
and doesn't have a job.

131
00:07:40,390 --> 00:07:41,780
Living here long-term,

132
00:07:41,870 --> 00:07:43,369
she won't be able to afford it.

133
00:07:43,370 --> 00:07:44,970
I'll give you a 50% discount.

134
00:07:45,810 --> 00:07:47,239
I don't think that's a good idea.

135
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:48,240
It's okay.

136
00:07:48,310 --> 00:07:49,310
Just move in.
Consider it

137
00:07:49,810 --> 00:07:51,219
tuition for teaching me

138
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:52,070
how to make desserts.

139
00:07:52,071 --> 00:07:53,509
No, I can't.

140
00:07:53,510 --> 00:07:54,510
It's really okay.

141
00:07:54,570 --> 00:07:56,239
Don't worry about the money.

142
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,369
You can pay me back slowly

143
00:07:57,370 --> 00:07:58,830
after you find a job.

144
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:01,039
Since Xia said so,

145
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:02,220
just stay here.

146
00:08:04,830 --> 00:08:06,629
Then thank you, Xia.

147
00:08:06,630 --> 00:08:07,540
Once I get an internship,

148
00:08:07,541 --> 00:08:08,929
I'll pay the rent.

149
00:08:08,930 --> 00:08:10,040
It's fine. No rush.

150
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,240
Great.

151
00:08:12,270 --> 00:08:13,270
Lili, if you live here,

152
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:13,870
we can

153
00:08:13,871 --> 00:08:14,929
go to school together.

154
00:08:14,930 --> 00:08:16,129
What's so good about it?

155
00:08:16,130 --> 00:08:17,270
I'm warning you,

156
00:08:17,510 --> 00:08:18,719
people like you who hit on girls

157
00:08:18,720 --> 00:08:20,009
and ask for their WeChat

158
00:08:20,010 --> 00:08:21,269
should stay away from our Lili.

159
00:08:21,270 --> 00:08:23,100
I'd call this fate with Lili.

160
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:26,269
You're destined to cross paths

161
00:08:26,270 --> 00:08:27,429
with every pretty girl.

162
00:08:27,430 --> 00:08:28,430
Xia Congsheng,

163
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:30,906
when Sang Zhi and I
had our parents called in,

164
00:08:30,930 --> 00:08:32,369
you thought her brother was handsome

165
00:08:32,370 --> 00:08:34,429
and asked for his WeChat, didn't you?

166
00:08:35,530 --> 00:08:37,059
Why are you bringing him up?

167
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:46,120
Speaking of WeChat,

168
00:08:46,820 --> 00:08:47,510
our Lili

169
00:08:47,511 --> 00:08:49,129
has never taken the initiative

170
00:08:49,130 --> 00:08:50,940
to ask for someone's WeChat.

171
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:57,200
Actually, I have.

172
00:08:58,650 --> 00:08:59,750
When?

173
00:09:00,010 --> 00:09:01,270
How come I didn't know?

174
00:09:02,290 --> 00:09:03,370
Is he handsome?

175
00:09:08,650 --> 00:09:09,650
Yeah.

176
00:09:10,860 --> 00:09:11,860
Did you add him?

177
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:15,670
No, I didn't.

178
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:17,900
Someone actually rejected you?

179
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:19,040
What happened?
Tell us,

180
00:09:19,750 --> 00:09:20,880
so we can analyze it.

181
00:09:21,410 --> 00:09:22,410
It's nothing.

182
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:24,620
Maybe it's my own problem.

183
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,219
How could it be your problem?

184
00:09:26,220 --> 00:09:27,820
It must be the guy's problem.

185
00:09:28,510 --> 00:09:29,830
How could it be
the guy's problem?

186
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:31,530
It must be the girl's...

187
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:36,889
It's definitely the guy's problem.

188
00:09:36,890 --> 00:09:38,150
And it's a big problem.

189
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:40,860
A big problem!

190
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:43,789
Maybe it's the first time

191
00:09:43,790 --> 00:09:45,099
this guy has been asked

192
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:46,339
for his WeChat by such a pretty girl.

193
00:09:46,340 --> 00:09:47,789
He wanted to play hard to get,

194
00:09:47,790 --> 00:09:49,590
but now he must be regretting it.

195
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:51,360
Yeah.

196
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:52,240
He must be kicking himself

197
00:09:52,241 --> 00:09:53,750
right now.

198
00:09:55,250 --> 00:09:56,250
But Lili,

199
00:09:56,460 --> 00:09:58,099
could it be because the guy

200
00:09:58,100 --> 00:09:59,100
has a girlfriend?

201
00:10:02,630 --> 00:10:03,790
Right, Uncle?

202
00:10:16,620 --> 00:10:17,620
Is it possible

203
00:10:18,030 --> 00:10:19,560
that when he said "No need,"

204
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,530
he meant the cold medicine?

205
00:10:31,100 --> 00:10:32,340
What cold medicine?

206
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:37,620
How about

207
00:10:37,621 --> 00:10:38,820
we add each other now?

208
00:10:38,940 --> 00:10:40,540
I promise I won't reject you.

209
00:10:42,310 --> 00:10:43,310
Lili.

210
00:10:44,050 --> 00:10:45,030
Let me add you on WeChat.

211
00:10:45,031 --> 00:10:46,490
I won't reject you either.

212
00:10:47,210 --> 00:10:49,050
Haven't we already?

213
00:10:50,290 --> 00:10:51,100
Last time,

214
00:10:51,101 --> 00:10:52,300
it was my alt account.

215
00:10:52,700 --> 00:10:54,030
You have an alt account?

216
00:10:54,630 --> 00:10:55,630
Such a player.

217
00:10:56,500 --> 00:10:57,960
It's the store's account.

218
00:10:58,790 --> 00:11:00,450
You two should add each other.

219
00:11:00,530 --> 00:11:01,790
No.

220
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:03,200
Uncle.

221
00:11:03,270 --> 00:11:04,930
Uncle, you should add her too.

222
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:09,789
Don't bother him.

223
00:11:09,790 --> 00:11:11,520
He doesn't like to join the fun.

224
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:43,440
I actually added him.

225
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:10,220
How is it?
I'm not bad, am I?

226
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:12,739
You didn't want to go before.

227
00:12:12,740 --> 00:12:13,790
Now you are happy.

228
00:12:14,790 --> 00:12:16,529
So he wasn't rejecting me.

229
00:12:16,530 --> 00:12:18,530
He was rejecting the cold medicine.

230
00:12:20,030 --> 00:12:21,250
No wonder.

231
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:23,199
I thought you two looked weird just now.

232
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:25,039
So that's how you two are connected.

233
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:26,099
It's not like that.

234
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:28,390
W-We just chatted a bit, and that's all.

235
00:12:28,790 --> 00:12:30,460
That wouldn't be enough.

236
00:12:31,550 --> 00:12:32,240
Anyway, now

237
00:12:32,241 --> 00:12:33,289
you've added each other on WeChat.

238
00:12:33,290 --> 00:12:34,499
Chat more when you are free,

239
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:36,240
and the feelings will grow.

240
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:39,340
In a relationship,

241
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:42,099
the most important thing is communication.

242
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:43,676
You have to chat more.
What relationship?

243
00:12:43,700 --> 00:12:45,560
How come we're in a relationship?

244
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:46,649
There's nothing to be shy about.

245
00:12:46,650 --> 00:12:47,340
This is a big step

246
00:12:47,341 --> 00:12:49,250
towards your happiness.

247
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:51,000
Be proactive.

248
00:12:53,130 --> 00:12:54,150
I'll try my best.

249
00:12:54,390 --> 00:12:55,390
Deal?

250
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:56,600
Deal.

251
00:12:56,940 --> 00:12:57,940
Deal.

252
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,000
Grandma.

253
00:13:08,530 --> 00:13:09,530
Time to eat.

254
00:13:09,790 --> 00:13:10,600
Look at you,

255
00:13:10,601 --> 00:13:11,790
sweating all over.

256
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,000
Wipe it.

257
00:13:14,790 --> 00:13:15,939
I have 2 boxes left.

258
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:17,420
I'll finish moving them soon.
No rush.

259
00:13:17,860 --> 00:13:18,630
Eat first.

260
00:13:18,631 --> 00:13:20,560
Move them after you finish eating.

261
00:13:25,100 --> 00:13:26,100
Here.

262
00:13:31,790 --> 00:13:33,240
Why is it chicken soup?

263
00:13:33,690 --> 00:13:35,090
Yuan loves fish.

264
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:42,240
I like both.

265
00:13:42,890 --> 00:13:44,220
I like chicken soup too.

266
00:13:45,740 --> 00:13:46,010
Here.

267
00:13:46,011 --> 00:13:47,070
Thank you, Auntie.

268
00:13:48,130 --> 00:13:50,060
It's Shize who loves chicken soup.

269
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:53,740
Why didn't Shize

270
00:13:53,741 --> 00:13:55,170
come to eat today?

271
00:13:55,510 --> 00:13:56,630
Did you two

272
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:57,840
have a fight?

273
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:00,120
No.

274
00:14:00,820 --> 00:14:01,820
We are good.

275
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:06,940
Shize is younger than you.

276
00:14:07,010 --> 00:14:08,270
You are older than him.

277
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:09,770
Give in to him more.

278
00:14:10,250 --> 00:14:11,250
Mm.

279
00:14:13,250 --> 00:14:14,860
Mom, you eat too.

280
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:16,960
I am eating.

281
00:14:17,150 --> 00:14:18,350
Here, Grandma, have some fish.

282
00:14:19,430 --> 00:14:20,890
Yuan, you're so sensible.

283
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:27,960
I'm full.

284
00:14:28,460 --> 00:14:30,120
I'll go to the front and check.

285
00:14:54,340 --> 00:14:55,340
Uncle,

286
00:14:55,750 --> 00:14:57,150
you'd better drink less.

287
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:59,360
It's bad for your health.

288
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:03,080
In the future,

289
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:05,500
don't come to our house often.

290
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:19,160
Who are you doing this for?

291
00:15:23,530 --> 00:15:25,000
No matter how much you do,

292
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,550
no one will forgive you!

293
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:34,760
Alright, alright.

294
00:15:35,030 --> 00:15:35,790
It's already the end of the month.

295
00:15:35,791 --> 00:15:36,939
Go settle the beer bill,

296
00:15:36,940 --> 00:15:38,030
will you?

297
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:48,960
Shize,

298
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:51,340
your uncle didn't mean that.

299
00:15:51,460 --> 00:15:52,790
Don't take it to heart.

300
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,700
Mm, I know.

301
00:15:56,460 --> 00:15:58,629
Some things can't be resolved

302
00:15:58,630 --> 00:15:59,790
in a day or two.

303
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:01,690
Just give him some time.

304
00:16:05,790 --> 00:16:06,790
By the way,

305
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:07,890
remember to give Grandma

306
00:16:07,891 --> 00:16:09,150
her medicine on time.

307
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:10,050
I've already transferred

308
00:16:10,051 --> 00:16:11,359
the money for this month.

309
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:12,340
Didn't I tell you

310
00:16:12,341 --> 00:16:13,529
not to send any more money?

311
00:16:13,530 --> 00:16:15,190
I'll go keep Grandma company.

312
00:16:16,750 --> 00:16:17,750
Hey.

313
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:22,650
This kid...

314
00:16:23,750 --> 00:16:24,750
Mom.

315
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:38,999
I've told you so many times.

316
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:39,600
Leave these chores

317
00:16:39,601 --> 00:16:40,790
to me from now on.

318
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:44,870
You and Dad

319
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:46,960
just need to enjoy your retirement.

320
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:29,709
There really is such a thing

321
00:17:29,710 --> 00:17:32,200
as the moon falling from the sky.

322
00:17:37,170 --> 00:17:38,590
Strange.

323
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,460
Not a single daily post.

324
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,310
What exactly have you been doing?

325
00:17:51,530 --> 00:17:53,600
[EAW Compute Platform]
Data connected.

326
00:17:53,601 --> 00:17:54,900
Start uploading.

327
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:10,940
Uploading.

328
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:24,610
Data transmission successful.

329
00:18:31,090 --> 00:18:31,980
I'm still busy,

330
00:18:32,110 --> 00:18:33,330
so I won't go to eat.

331
00:18:34,410 --> 00:18:35,720
I can't write my paper,

332
00:18:35,850 --> 00:18:37,380
so I'm not in the mood to eat.

333
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:39,160
Yuan,

334
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:41,060
I'll bring you some food.

335
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:05,500
Yuan.

336
00:19:06,010 --> 00:19:07,439
You haven't eaten yet, right?

337
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:08,770
Look what I brought you.

338
00:19:13,740 --> 00:19:14,740
Try it.

339
00:19:18,830 --> 00:19:19,830
Eat.

340
00:19:29,550 --> 00:19:32,960
Is Professor Che still
rushing you for your paper?

341
00:19:38,510 --> 00:19:40,310
Doesn't he know your situation?

342
00:19:40,500 --> 00:19:41,500
It's fine.

343
00:19:41,900 --> 00:19:44,430
I don't really want to bother him.

344
00:19:46,700 --> 00:19:48,699
I've been taking my
medicine on time lately,

345
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:50,300
and I'm feeling much better.

346
00:19:50,790 --> 00:19:51,790
Really.

347
00:19:56,290 --> 00:19:57,000
By the way, Yuan,

348
00:19:57,001 --> 00:19:58,640
I have another paper

349
00:19:59,240 --> 00:20:00,509
that has already been edited.

350
00:20:00,510 --> 00:20:02,659
It should be able to get
into a top-tier journal.

351
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:04,589
Since you wrote the algorithm anyway,

352
00:20:04,590 --> 00:20:07,249
I was considering listing
you as the first author,

353
00:20:07,250 --> 00:20:08,659
with Professor Che as corresponding author.

354
00:20:08,660 --> 00:20:10,860
That way, you can submit your paper too.

355
00:20:14,270 --> 00:20:15,270
No need.

356
00:20:16,090 --> 00:20:17,820
Professor Shi agreed to it too.

357
00:20:22,740 --> 00:20:23,759
I-It's fine, Yuan.

358
00:20:23,760 --> 00:20:25,370
I said "No need"!

359
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:27,350
I know you're excellent.

360
00:20:28,290 --> 00:20:29,550
I don't need your help.

361
00:20:32,590 --> 00:20:33,590
Do you...

362
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,400
also think I can't do it?

363
00:20:39,250 --> 00:20:40,460
Are you pitying me?

364
00:20:45,660 --> 00:20:46,660
Sorry, Yuan.
I...

365
00:20:48,220 --> 00:20:49,530
I didn't mean that.

366
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:53,080
I just wanted to help you.

367
00:20:53,660 --> 00:20:54,660
Just like...

368
00:20:55,050 --> 00:20:56,696
Just like how you helped me
when we were kids.

369
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:57,720
I don't need it!

370
00:21:00,940 --> 00:21:01,940
I don't need it.

371
00:21:11,420 --> 00:21:12,880
I can handle my own affairs

372
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:14,960
by myself.

373
00:21:16,370 --> 00:21:17,900
I don't need anyone's pity.

374
00:22:05,220 --> 00:22:06,220
Yuan.

375
00:22:07,410 --> 00:22:08,410
Hang in there!

376
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:10,499
The ambulance will be here soon.

377
00:22:10,500 --> 00:22:11,500
Hold on, Yuan!

378
00:22:33,830 --> 00:22:35,720
What exactly happened?

379
00:22:35,830 --> 00:22:37,090
How could this happen?

380
00:22:38,010 --> 00:22:39,340
What exactly happened?

381
00:22:40,180 --> 00:22:41,180
Say something!

382
00:22:41,610 --> 00:22:42,610
Uncle,

383
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:45,680
Yuan...

384
00:22:49,270 --> 00:22:50,659
Doctor! Doctor!

385
00:22:50,660 --> 00:22:51,679
-Doctor! -Doctor!

386
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:52,680
Doctor,

387
00:22:52,720 --> 00:22:53,980
how is my son?

388
00:22:54,070 --> 00:22:54,740
Please calm down.

389
00:22:54,741 --> 00:22:56,740
The doctors are resuscitating him.

390
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:03,240
Fu Shize!

391
00:23:03,420 --> 00:23:04,939
Because of his depression,

392
00:23:04,940 --> 00:23:06,549
the doctor suggested he
take a break from school.

393
00:23:06,550 --> 00:23:08,219
You promised us you would take care of him

394
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:09,699
and make sure he would
take his medicine properly.

395
00:23:09,700 --> 00:23:11,939
That's why we agreed to
let him continue his PhD.

396
00:23:11,940 --> 00:23:13,670
Is this how you take care of him?

397
00:23:19,830 --> 00:23:20,830
I'm sorry.

398
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:22,560
What's the use of being sorry?

399
00:23:22,940 --> 00:23:24,880
You never really cared about him!

400
00:23:25,220 --> 00:23:27,310
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

401
00:23:27,880 --> 00:23:28,880
Get lost!

402
00:23:30,770 --> 00:23:31,770
Get lost!

403
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:33,680
Get lost!

404
00:25:05,420 --> 00:25:06,420
Yuan.

405
00:25:08,010 --> 00:25:09,460
I came to see you.

406
00:25:12,480 --> 00:25:14,890
[Tomb of Beloved Son Jiang Yuan]

407
00:25:52,270 --> 00:25:54,000
You don't like the rain either,

408
00:25:55,810 --> 00:25:56,810
do you?

409
00:26:11,090 --> 00:26:12,090
Fu Shize,

410
00:26:12,210 --> 00:26:12,910
I'm going to send you

411
00:26:12,911 --> 00:26:14,740
the first message.

412
00:26:19,590 --> 00:26:21,610
Nice to meet you.

413
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:26,210
Isn't that too robotic?

414
00:26:26,570 --> 00:26:27,570
No,

415
00:26:27,770 --> 00:26:28,830
this won't work.

416
00:26:31,530 --> 00:26:32,740
Nice to meet you.

417
00:26:32,810 --> 00:26:35,410
I would appreciate your
guidance and support.

418
00:26:36,610 --> 00:26:38,830
T-This is too pretentious.

419
00:26:45,250 --> 00:26:46,250
Good night.

420
00:26:49,240 --> 00:26:52,100
Does anyone say good night
for their first message?

421
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:53,440
I don't think so.

422
00:26:57,380 --> 00:26:59,240
Send a sticker.

423
00:27:00,680 --> 00:27:02,740
There isn't any suitable one either.

424
00:27:24,090 --> 00:27:25,350
In the office at night?

425
00:27:34,640 --> 00:27:35,640
No way.

426
00:27:42,730 --> 00:27:48,450
[You've got a Weixin message.]

427
00:28:13,220 --> 00:28:16,480
Who sent me a message so late?

428
00:28:23,330 --> 00:28:25,529
Fu Shize took the initiative to message me.

429
00:28:25,530 --> 00:28:26,920
Am I dreaming?

430
00:28:33,450 --> 00:28:34,950
Be my wife.

431
00:28:40,680 --> 00:28:42,080
Recall. Recall. Recall.

432
00:28:43,720 --> 00:28:44,810
I can't recall it!

433
00:28:45,310 --> 00:28:46,570
How could this happen?

434
00:28:47,140 --> 00:28:48,140
What happened?

435
00:28:55,700 --> 00:28:59,770
[Two minutes ago]

436
00:29:11,980 --> 00:29:13,529
Since things have come to this,

437
00:29:13,530 --> 00:29:14,570
let me explain.

438
00:29:25,770 --> 00:29:27,200
I pressed it by mistake.

439
00:29:27,220 --> 00:29:28,220
Sorry.

440
00:29:40,010 --> 00:29:41,270
Yun Li.

441
00:30:40,570 --> 00:30:42,790
What does "Mm" mean?

442
00:30:51,140 --> 00:30:52,140
Tangy?

443
00:30:53,070 --> 00:30:54,590
Why are you here so early?

444
00:30:54,620 --> 00:30:55,989
Did you stay up all night?

445
00:30:55,990 --> 00:30:57,529
Your dark circles are so heavy.

446
00:30:57,530 --> 00:30:59,570
I didn't sleep well last night.

447
00:31:01,530 --> 00:31:03,420
Why did you come so early?

448
00:31:03,680 --> 00:31:04,540
Did you forget?

449
00:31:04,570 --> 00:31:06,230
I said I'd help you move today.

450
00:31:08,380 --> 00:31:09,719
Moving today?

451
00:31:09,720 --> 00:31:10,720
Yeah.

452
00:31:16,700 --> 00:31:17,230
Let's go.

453
00:31:17,400 --> 00:31:18,720
Let me recharge you.

454
00:31:27,800 --> 00:31:28,930
Where are you going?

455
00:31:28,940 --> 00:31:30,000
I'm going to Nanwu.

456
00:31:30,220 --> 00:31:31,680
Why are you going to Nanwu?

457
00:31:32,140 --> 00:31:33,560
To bring Yun Li back.

458
00:31:35,240 --> 00:31:36,829
I know you love your daughter,

459
00:31:36,830 --> 00:31:38,570
but she's grown up.

460
00:31:38,850 --> 00:31:39,380
You can't always

461
00:31:39,381 --> 00:31:40,639
hold her to the standards

462
00:31:40,640 --> 00:31:41,640
of a little child.

463
00:31:42,380 --> 00:31:43,700
Besides,
if you go just like that,

464
00:31:44,180 --> 00:31:45,879
are you sure she'll come back with you?

465
00:31:45,880 --> 00:31:46,880
If she won't,

466
00:31:46,881 --> 00:31:48,680
I'll tie her up and drag her back.

467
00:31:49,070 --> 00:31:50,070
Look at you,

468
00:31:50,140 --> 00:31:51,570
getting all worked up.

469
00:31:51,920 --> 00:31:53,679
If you hadn't been so ill-tempered,

470
00:31:53,680 --> 00:31:55,269
would she have stayed away this long?

471
00:31:55,270 --> 00:31:57,309
Yun Li has been gone for so many days.

472
00:31:57,310 --> 00:31:58,180
As her mother,

473
00:31:58,181 --> 00:31:59,810
aren't you worried?

474
00:32:00,310 --> 00:32:01,640
Why should I be worried?

475
00:32:01,880 --> 00:32:03,180
I trust my daughter.

476
00:32:03,610 --> 00:32:04,610
Why?

477
00:32:04,920 --> 00:32:05,920
You don't?

478
00:32:06,130 --> 00:32:06,780
I...

479
00:32:06,800 --> 00:32:08,260
Let's not talk about this.

480
00:32:08,440 --> 00:32:09,720
Where are you going?

481
00:32:10,690 --> 00:32:11,690
To buy breakfast.

482
00:32:12,010 --> 00:32:13,010
Right.
Come back!

483
00:32:16,060 --> 00:32:17,219
Breakfast is on the table.

484
00:32:17,220 --> 00:32:18,620
What are you going to buy?

485
00:32:22,740 --> 00:32:24,070
Let me tell you, Yun Ye,

486
00:32:24,810 --> 00:32:25,829
don't learn from your sister.

487
00:32:25,830 --> 00:32:27,289
You only pick up bad habits!

488
00:32:27,290 --> 00:32:28,290
Alright.
Hurry up and eat.

489
00:32:28,580 --> 00:32:29,580
It'll get cold.

490
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:32,040
Take your dad's luggage inside.

491
00:32:35,450 --> 00:32:36,000
I'm telling you,

492
00:32:36,001 --> 00:32:37,699
if you take your sister's side again,

493
00:32:37,700 --> 00:32:39,639
don't even think about
getting pocket money!

494
00:32:39,640 --> 00:32:41,440
Time to eat.

495
00:32:47,500 --> 00:32:49,220
If Dad treats Li like this,

496
00:32:49,400 --> 00:32:51,330
he'll definitely be harsher on me.

497
00:32:51,980 --> 00:32:52,510
No way.

498
00:32:52,830 --> 00:32:54,160
I need to prepare early.

499
00:33:01,400 --> 00:33:02,840
Hello, your food is ready.
Thank you.

500
00:33:11,510 --> 00:33:12,990
What are you looking at?

501
00:33:13,220 --> 00:33:14,220
Give it back.

502
00:33:16,350 --> 00:33:17,699
You've grown up,

503
00:33:17,700 --> 00:33:18,960
with your own secrets.

504
00:33:19,030 --> 00:33:21,360
I don't even know what you were looking at.

505
00:33:35,790 --> 00:33:37,330
Wow, look at you.

506
00:33:37,900 --> 00:33:39,830
"Be my wife."

507
00:33:41,440 --> 00:33:42,749
It's really embarrassing.

508
00:33:42,750 --> 00:33:43,160
My...

509
00:33:43,161 --> 00:33:44,899
My hand slipped, and I sent it by accident.

510
00:33:44,900 --> 00:33:46,589
I think you're sly.

511
00:33:46,590 --> 00:33:47,460
My hand really slipped.

512
00:33:47,461 --> 00:33:48,750
It was just sent...

513
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:51,290
Tangy,

514
00:33:51,291 --> 00:33:52,739
how about we don't move today?

515
00:33:52,740 --> 00:33:54,589
It'll be so awkward if we run into him.

516
00:33:54,590 --> 00:33:56,450
What's there to be awkward about?

517
00:33:57,440 --> 00:33:58,790
It is. I...

518
00:34:01,330 --> 00:34:02,330
How about this?

519
00:34:11,010 --> 00:34:12,010
Next time you see him,

520
00:34:12,400 --> 00:34:13,400
you can say,

521
00:34:13,610 --> 00:34:14,649
"Hello, Honey."

522
00:34:14,650 --> 00:34:15,759
"Honey."

523
00:34:15,760 --> 00:34:17,000
"Honey, I'm over here."
"Honey."

524
00:34:17,150 --> 00:34:17,900
Tang Lin.

525
00:34:18,050 --> 00:34:19,440
Be serious.

526
00:34:19,750 --> 00:34:20,750
Alright.

527
00:34:27,040 --> 00:34:28,859
I almost forgot the real business.

528
00:34:28,860 --> 00:34:29,959
Didn't you tell me yesterday

529
00:34:29,960 --> 00:34:31,399
that you wanted to find an internship?

530
00:34:31,400 --> 00:34:32,459
I found some companies for you.

531
00:34:32,460 --> 00:34:33,900
And Xia found some too.

532
00:34:34,050 --> 00:34:34,840
I'll send them to you later.

533
00:34:34,841 --> 00:34:36,370
Let's take a look together.

534
00:34:36,590 --> 00:34:37,000
It seems

535
00:34:37,001 --> 00:34:38,340
EAW is also hiring.

536
00:34:38,400 --> 00:34:39,839
Why don't you just go there?

537
00:34:39,840 --> 00:34:41,359
That way, you'll have an
acquaintance looking out for you,

538
00:34:41,360 --> 00:34:42,460
including your...

539
00:34:43,280 --> 00:34:45,420
honey.

540
00:34:45,960 --> 00:34:47,089
I'm not listening.

541
00:34:47,090 --> 00:34:48,090
Honey.

542
00:34:48,280 --> 00:34:49,820
Honey.

543
00:35:13,340 --> 00:35:14,800
Have you thought about it?

544
00:35:18,470 --> 00:35:19,670
Are you coming or not?

545
00:35:19,690 --> 00:35:21,150
Give me a definite answer.

546
00:35:21,820 --> 00:35:22,820
Mm.

547
00:35:22,900 --> 00:35:24,360
What does that mean?

548
00:35:24,760 --> 00:35:25,960
Are you coming or not?

549
00:35:29,400 --> 00:35:31,200
Exactly what you think it means.

550
00:35:32,550 --> 00:35:33,860
So you agree, right?

551
00:35:36,280 --> 00:35:37,550
I'll take that as a yes!

552
00:35:46,820 --> 00:35:48,420
Welcome to the Light Chaser.

553
00:35:51,260 --> 00:35:52,399
MLP node

554
00:35:52,400 --> 00:35:53,600
connections normal.

555
00:35:54,500 --> 00:35:56,230
System self-check completed.

556
00:35:56,800 --> 00:35:59,400
You are about to embark
on a journey of wonders.

557
00:36:34,860 --> 00:36:37,030
Program loading is ready.

558
00:36:38,320 --> 00:36:39,710
Ready for departure.

559
00:36:47,360 --> 00:36:48,879
Arrived at the destination.

560
00:36:48,880 --> 00:36:50,810
Preparing for lunar exploration.

561
00:38:24,050 --> 00:38:25,839
I told you not to bring these things.

562
00:38:25,840 --> 00:38:27,440
Why did you still bring them?

563
00:38:27,460 --> 00:38:28,499
They are all daily necessities.

564
00:38:28,500 --> 00:38:29,629
You will always find a use for them.

565
00:38:29,630 --> 00:38:30,830
We should save money.

566
00:38:30,900 --> 00:38:32,030
Why spend it?

567
00:38:34,030 --> 00:38:35,230
Puppy, open the door.

568
00:38:36,960 --> 00:38:38,190
Puppy, open the door.

569
00:38:39,130 --> 00:38:40,370
Coming! Coming!

570
00:38:43,910 --> 00:38:45,510
Who were you calling a puppy?

571
00:38:46,860 --> 00:38:47,860
Lili, good morning.

572
00:38:48,730 --> 00:38:50,250
Good morning.
Is there anyone else here

573
00:38:50,300 --> 00:38:51,340
besides you?
Be a good boy.

574
00:38:51,980 --> 00:38:53,730
Bark for me.

575
00:38:55,290 --> 00:38:55,950
Old Auntie,

576
00:38:55,960 --> 00:38:57,220
I advise you to be kind.

577
00:38:57,530 --> 00:38:58,530
You...
You're here.

578
00:38:59,340 --> 00:39:00,340
Xia.

579
00:39:01,030 --> 00:39:02,106
Let me help you with that.
Come on,

580
00:39:02,130 --> 00:39:03,460
I'll show you your room.

581
00:39:03,760 --> 00:39:04,760
Thank you.

582
00:39:06,600 --> 00:39:07,270
Zhengchu,

583
00:39:07,290 --> 00:39:08,959
help Tangy with her things too.

584
00:39:08,960 --> 00:39:09,960
Okay.

585
00:39:10,800 --> 00:39:11,800
Give it to me.
No need.

586
00:39:12,150 --> 00:39:13,350
I can carry it myself.

587
00:39:18,030 --> 00:39:19,030
Move aside.

588
00:39:25,970 --> 00:39:26,970
Just give it to me.

589
00:39:27,050 --> 00:39:28,850
With your old arms and legs,
don't fall later.

590
00:39:37,360 --> 00:39:38,620
The room is over there.

591
00:39:38,840 --> 00:39:39,929
Make yourself at home.

592
00:39:39,930 --> 00:39:41,530
Make yourself comfortable.

593
00:39:52,090 --> 00:39:52,760
This conditioner

594
00:39:52,761 --> 00:39:54,049
makes your hair really smooth.

595
00:39:54,050 --> 00:39:55,439
And this scalp serum

596
00:39:55,440 --> 00:39:57,000
works really well too.
You can try them.

597
00:39:57,360 --> 00:39:58,730
You brought too much.

598
00:40:02,340 --> 00:40:03,549
This guesthouse is great,

599
00:40:03,550 --> 00:40:04,759
except that it doesn't have a wardrobe.

600
00:40:04,760 --> 00:40:06,759
What will you do with all your clothes?

601
00:40:06,760 --> 00:40:07,630
As long as I have a place to stay,

602
00:40:07,631 --> 00:40:08,799
I don't ask for much.

603
00:40:08,800 --> 00:40:09,800
That won't do.

604
00:40:09,940 --> 00:40:10,959
How about we go buy one later?

605
00:40:10,960 --> 00:40:12,360
No need.
I'll just put them there...

606
00:40:12,630 --> 00:40:13,630
Lili.

607
00:40:19,440 --> 00:40:20,130
Girls have a lot of stuff,

608
00:40:20,131 --> 00:40:21,189
so I brought this over for you.

609
00:40:21,190 --> 00:40:22,359
Lili, where should I put it?

610
00:40:22,360 --> 00:40:23,480
It's fine.
Just put it there.

611
00:40:23,940 --> 00:40:24,940
Thank you.

612
00:40:25,630 --> 00:40:27,230
Call me if you need anything.

613
00:40:30,800 --> 00:40:32,566
Right.
Congsheng said there's a welcome dinner

614
00:40:32,590 --> 00:40:33,190
tonight.

615
00:40:33,191 --> 00:40:34,590
We're having a barbecue.

616
00:40:34,940 --> 00:40:36,000
You should join us.

617
00:41:01,500 --> 00:41:02,500
Uncle.

618
00:41:02,610 --> 00:41:03,859
Come eat at the guesthouse tonight.

619
00:41:03,860 --> 00:41:04,979
Congsheng is throwing a party.

620
00:41:04,980 --> 00:41:06,050
You guys go ahead.

621
00:41:07,010 --> 00:41:08,650
Lili is moving in tonight.

622
00:41:09,090 --> 00:41:10,290
Why don't you join us?

623
00:41:11,110 --> 00:41:12,110
Uncle, come on.

624
00:41:16,110 --> 00:41:17,110
We'll see.

625
00:41:19,260 --> 00:41:20,050
Well?

626
00:41:20,070 --> 00:41:21,460
Is Uncle coming?

627
00:41:22,260 --> 00:41:23,320
He said he would see.

